<title>TURKEY: Turkish Erciyas H1 profits fall.</title>
<headline>Turkish Erciyas H1 profits fall.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>January-June 1997 final</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>				    H1 1997	   H1 1996</p>
<p>				    -------	   -------</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)    83.95  vs   2,540.79</p>
<p>    Net profit		    251.86  vs   1,905.59</p>
<p>    Net sales		   6,551.32  vs   3,798.84</p>
<p>    Operating profit	  1,789.63  vs     991.60</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	1,276.87  vs   2,280.64</p>
<p>    Interest paid	     2,243.54  vs	28.47</p>
<p>    Total debts		12,092.67  vs   7,186.49</p>
<p>    Equity			6,664.75  vs   6,247.50</p>
<p>    Capital		     3,000.00  vs     750.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Shares of Turkish brewer Erciyas Biracilik ve Malt Sanayii A.S are also traded in SEAQ International in London and over the counter NASDAQ market in the U.S.A.</p>
<p>Largely owned by Turkish brewery, automotive and stationary group Anadolu Endustri Holding, Erciyas Produces leading Efes Pilsen brand with three other brewers within the same group.</p>
<p>It participated in Efes Technic Consultancy Limited by 30 percent on May.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 78 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in June.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212 275 08 75</p>
</text>
